-- title:
--   Gauss valuation and prime p at a finite-chart point
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M\neq 0$ with $p\mid M$ and $p^{2}\nmid M$, and a subgroup $H\le(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ containing every unit whose image in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^{\times}$ is trivial; assume the $q$-expansion `jqModC` of $j$ lies in the field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`. Given a model datum $\mathfrak{X}$ of type `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` over $R_p=\mathbb{Q}$-numbers with denominator prime to $p$, let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of the function field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (ΓM M H)` consisting exactly of those $f_0$ for which there are power series $a,a'$ with coefficients in $R_p$, with $a'$ not reducing to $0$ modulo $p$, such that $f_0\cdot a'=a$ as Laurent series (the Gauss valuation ring). Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit in $A$, residue field algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and $\rho:R_p\to A$ a ring map compatible with the structure map to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $y$ be a point of the fibre of `toBase p (ΓM M H) hj` over the residue field of $A$ via $\rho$, lying in the image of the base map of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}$ at index $0$ but not at index $1$, and let $\mathfrak{p}$ be a prime of the finite chart algebra `chartAlgFin p (ΓM M H) hj` whose image under $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}$ is the first projection of $y$. Then: the image of $p$ lies in $\mathfrak{p}$; for every $s\notin\mathfrak{p}$ the inverse of $s$ in the function field lies in $W_0$; and the ideal generated by $p$ in `Localization.AtPrime 𝔭.asIdeal` is prime.
--
--   This is the finite ($j$-)chart local analysis of a Deligne–Rapoport style integral model at a point of the characteristic-$p$ fibre that lies on one of the two components of the special fibre and not the other: the local ring at such a point sits inside the Gauss valuation ring of $q$-expansions, and $p$ cuts out a prime there. It feeds the construction of regular $q$-expansions for cusp forms away from the supersingular places.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XHDRModelAtP_mem_gauss_and_isPrime_map_span_of_mem_range_comp_zero_of_not_mem_range_comp_one_chartAlgFin.lean

